      <node id="108194428751240116" label="108194428751240116">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '108194428751240116', 'username': 'sundogplanets', 'followers': 18457, 'following': 1498, 'bio': '&lt;p&gt;Professor of astronomy, farmer of goats.  Asteroid (42910).  She/her.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Living and learning on the land and under the skies of Treaty 4 (Saskatchewan, Canada).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Saskatchewan&amp;#39;s beautiful night sky, my research background in small body orbital dynamics, and a couple of really unfortunately placed SpaceX reentries, I spend a lot of time yelling about satellite pollution in international news media.&lt;/p&gt;', 'created_at': '2022-04-25 00:00:00'}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="108213490230287823" label="108213490230287823">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '108213490230287823', 'username': 'quirkystreets', 'followers': 92, 'following': 120, 'bio': '&lt;p&gt;My plant community is N. Cali Coastal Sage Scrub/Strand. My profile pic is a bunch of css lupines on a bike path. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Why native plants?&lt;br&gt;The local plants co-evolved with the local insects/birds/etc to make an ecosystem. Oak trees are a host plant for 150+ butterflies/moths, which start out as caterpillars, otherwise known as bird food. A nest of baby birds needs 600-900 worms to eat. A non-native plant hosts 0 insects, starving the birds. The bees like them too.&lt;/p&gt;', 'created_at': '2022-04-29 00:00:00'}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
